2. MXFP4 x FP8 GEMM  -- Apache-2.0 since 2026-09-22 (was listed as derived)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    kernels/r9k_moe_mxfp4a8.hip, kernels/r9k_gemm_fp8.hip,
    r9700_vllm/kernels/moe.py

    These were previously carved out as derived from libr4d by StillDeadcode
    (https://codeberg.org/StillDeadcode/libr4d). An audit on 2026-09-22 found
    that nothing in them is authored content we took:

      * kMag, the folded-unpack table, is GENERATED, not written. Run
        `tools/gen_kmag.py --check`: all 16 rows follow from the OCP e2m1 and
        e4m3 specifications plus one rounding convention.
      * the unpack's masks and shifts follow from the MXFP4 packing and the two
        format definitions; the v_perm selectors follow from V_PERM_B32's own
        semantics and from de-interleaving nibble-packed elements.
      * the fragment-order weight layout is FORCED by the gfx12 WMMA builtin --
        any correct implementation produces identical bytes.
      * in-block split-K through LDS is a textbook technique.
      * r9k_gemm_fp8.hip contains no folded code at all (it is fp8 x fp8, with
        nothing to unpack).

    What libr4d arrived at first is the folded-exponent *method* -- fold the
    block exponent into the e4m3 operand, carry 2^(Wref-127) to the epilogue.
    A method is not copyrightable expression. The audit establishing that, and
    the generator that reproduces the table, are in notes/independence.md and
    tools/gen_kmag.py.

    Headers and SPDX identifiers on these files were corrected accordingly.

