5. Runtime dependencies  -- not redistributed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    vLLM, ROCm, PyTorch and Triton are used unmodified at runtime and are not
    included here.

    libr4d's binary (r4d.so) is NOT redistributed by this repository
    (.gitignore excludes *.so) and, since 2026-09-22, is NOT USED AT ALL by the
    default configuration: paged attention and the 2-rank all-reduce are both
    our own kernels. Verified by moving r4d.so aside and serving without it.
    R9K_PAGED_ATTN=r4d and R9K_AR_IMPL=r4d still select libr4d's versions for
    A/B comparison, if you have that library.

    So the ONLY libr4d exposure left in this repository is the derived GEMM
    source in item 2 above -- a licensing question, not a runtime dependency.

See CREDITS.md for the third-party components, and notes/independence.md for the
provenance of the kernels -- what was replaced with original work, what each
piece is measurably worth, and which constants are generated from published
format specifications rather than authored.
